window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>The Forgotten Code: Summary</p> <p>In the National Archives, cryptographer Dr. Evelyn Reed uncovers a modern conspiracy hidden within an 1814 letter's cipher: FOUNDATION PROTOCOL ACTIVATION IMMINENT. PHASE ONE TARGET: CAPITOL HILL. Her discovery triggers a remote system wipe and a chilling threat, marking her for elimination by a powerful, unknown enemy.</p> <p>Disillusioned FBI Agent Marcus Jones, investigating the breach, finds Evelyn's terrifying claims validated when they decode microscopic engravings on the letter, revealing a NEUTRALIZE list of officials and pinpointing the mastermind: untouchable Senator Silas Stealth.</p> <p>Forced to flee, framed by media leaks, and hunted by Stealth's shadowy \"Foundation,\" Evelyn and Marcus race against time. Their only hope lies in deciphering the rest of the engravings, which detail the full coup plot set for Inauguration Day. They discover Stealth is twisting history, using the original cipher creator's patriotic contingency plan as justification for his own violent power grab.</p> <p>Pursued through D.C., Evelyn's cryptographic genius and Marcus's tactical skills are their only weapons. From desperate gambles with Cold War comms techniques to infiltrating the U.S. Capitol itself hours before the attack, they must expose the plot before explosives detonate and democracy falls. Can they unravel a conspiracy centuries in the making and stop a tyrant hiding in plain sight? The Forgotten Code holds the answer, but time is running out.</p>"; 
